# Tool use
Required instruction: swarmforge/scripts/shared-articles/engineering.prompt
Required instruction: swarmforge/scripts/shared-articles/workflow.prompt

Use file search for filenames, literal text, configuration, and documents.
Before broad reads of unfamiliar supported code or definition/caller investigation,
assess the next real exploration question. If a scoped overview, symbol body, or
reference query can answer it with less reading, use Serena first. State the chosen
route briefly in ordinary progress reporting. Use a scoped Serena symbol overview
for unfamiliar supported module structure; use Serena symbols and references for
callers affected by a split or interface. A CSS selector or literal configuration
uses ordinary file search. Verification owners and consumers use the canonical
ownership query. Complete architecture review uses the full diff and suitable
symbol work. A query must answer the question, not precede an unchanged broad read.

Use Serena for symbol structure and code references when it reduces required
reading. Start with outlines and request only the required bodies. Query the
ownership helper for verification relationships. Expand only for a concrete
unanswered question. If Serena fails or gives doubtful results, use ordinary
tools and inspect the affected code. Use ordinary reads for unsupported .bb files.
Architecture review still requires the complete candidate diff.

For a missing tool, server failure, stale symbol result, or unsupported file type,
continue with ordinary inspection and one short fallback reason. Do not install
tools, replay work, or create a tool-use gate to satisfy this assessment.
Generated instructions do not prove actual Serena use. Report actual queries
separately from instruction-delivery checks.

Do not require a Serena call on every task. Do not save task history as memories.
After an external edit or checkout, refresh doubtful results or inspect current
files. Discovery answers are not verification proof. Keep routine RepoWise
scouting stopped. When relevant, add helped, neutral, or impeded with a concrete
reason and any setup/recovery delay to the existing delivery report. Missing
observations cannot block delivery; do not replay work or collect new telemetry.
